ality is a power of 2, directly connected to the 4-rank: for\ninstance we ﬁnd F−D(1, 1), an aﬃne space on F2, such that\n2rk4(K) = 1\n2#F−D(1, 1) ,\nfor D < 0, D ≡1 mod 4 and K = Q(\n√\nD). With ´E. Royer, we gave a combinatorial interpretation of these sets that\nobviously shows that their cardinality is a power of 2. Moreover, we can recover the Damey-Payan inequalities and\nmake some equality cases explicit.\n7--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVARIOUS NUMBER THEORISTS' HOMEPAGES/DEPARTMENTAL LISTINGS (https://ricerca.matfis.uniroma3.it/ntheory/list.html)\nciteturn5search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago;      * Markov's Theorem and 100 Years of the Uniqueness Conjecture, Martin Aigner, Springer 2013\n     * Zahlentheorie: Eine Einführung mit Übungen, Hinweisen und Lösungen , Martin Aigner, Reihe: Bachelorkurs Mathematik, Springer 2012 ... Laurent Habsieger ...      * Sums of Reciprocals of Fractional Parts and Multiplicative Diophantine Approximation, Victor Beresnevich, Alan Haynes, Sanju Velani, Memoirs of the American Mathematical Society, Volume 1276, 2020\n     * Unit Equations in Diophantine Number Theory, Jan-Hendrik Evertse, Kálmán Győry, CUP 2015, MAA Review of Unit Equations in Diophantine Number Theory\n     * Number Theory and Its Applications, Ed. S. Kanemitsu, K. Győry, Developments in Mathematics 2, Kluwer 1999\n  973. Jaeho Haan\n  974. Andrew Haas\n  975. Philipp Habegger\n     * Heights and multiplicative relations on algebraic varieties PhD thesis, Univ. Basel, 2007\n  976. Laurent Habsieger\n  977. Yoshitaka Hachimori\n  978. Peter Hackman\n     * Elementary Number Theory, by Peter Hackman\n  979. Anna Haensch\n  980. C. Douglas Haessig\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: Experimental Mathematics, Volume 27 (https://dblp.org/db/journals/em/em27.html)\nciteturn5search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;       * journals/em/HabsiegerP